The '''Augusta Corridor''' ({{lang-it|Corridoio Agostino}}), also known as the '''Alessandria–Otranto metropolitan region''' ({{lang-it|Regione metropolitana di Lissandria–Otranto}}) is an emerging {{W|transborder agglomeration}} between [[Balisca]] and [[Siculia]]. It is the third most populous [[megaregions of Balisca|urbanate]] within the Baliscan Confederation after [[Concordia]] and the [[Solana|Solana Megalopolis]], with over 13 million residents (representing 9.75% of Balisca's total population). It includes the major cities of [[Alessandria]], [[Otranto]], and [[Castello]] along with their metropolitan areas and [[W:Satellite city|satellites]].

The largest centers of the urban area maintain {{W|global city}} status and as a whole the metropolitan region is host to ## consulates from Asian, European, North American, Oceanian, and South American nations. Over 20 million people cross the border each year between Alessandria and [[Otranto]] (via Castello), giving the region one of the busiest land-border crossings in the world. Since the end of the [[W:Cold War|Cold War]], Alessandria–Otranto has become a dominant commercial center in the {{W|South Atlantic Ocean|South Atlantic}}. The economic success of globalization has allowed Alessandria–Otranto to grow to become the third-wealthiest megalopolis in the region, with a GDP of $000.00 billion in 2023. Renowned for natural beauty, {{W|tourism}} is a leading industry in the region and its coastal environs have been paramount factors in the growth of action sports-lifestyle cooperatives. Other key industries include military, biotech, and manufacturing.

Alessandria–Otranto traces its European roots to the early 16th century when the land was explored by various Italian explorers on behalf of the {{W|Maritime republics}}. During these missions, explorers were able to map the Augustine coast in great detail, leading to the eventual settlement and the founding of the [[Hesperian League]]. In 2020, the [[2020 Mount Antonio eruption|eruption of Mount Antonio]] brought about significant increases in binational and inter-regional cooperation for the first time.

